From abe3b2b5b5fcfccadafda099b66437c1c39ae4cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakub Jelen <jjelen@redhat.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:50:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Update the upstream signing keys

Replace gpgkey-aide.gpg with gpgkey-aide.asc, the key upstream publishes
at
https://keys.openpgp.org/vks/v1/by-fingerprint/2BBBD30FAAB29B3253BCFBA6F6947DAB68E7B931#/gpgkey-aide.asc
(byte for byte); its Source line is now that URL.
Refresh nettle-release-keyring.gpg from keyservers: same certificate(s),
with self-signatures our copy was missing.
The commands are in the comment above its Source line.
nettle-release-keyring.gpg was in the lookaside cache, which a pull
request cannot update, so it moves into git (dropped from sources).

The current key is needed to verify the release signature with
openpgpverify (sqv), which checks that the key was valid when the
release was signed.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 .gitignore                 |   1 -
 aide.spec                  |   6 +-
 gpgkey-aide.asc            | 634 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 gpgkey-aide.gpg            | Bin 5160 -> 0 bytes
 nettle-release-keyring.gpg | 520 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 sources                    |   1 -
 6 files changed, 1157 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 gpgkey-aide.asc
 delete mode 100644 gpgkey-aide.gpg
 create mode 100644 nettle-release-keyring.gpg

